<title>ITALY: Italian mutual funds post Feb inflow, equities up.</title>
<headline>Italian mutual funds post Feb inflow, equities up.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian investment funds had a net inflow of 14.920 trillion lire in February, slightly down on a historic high net inflow of 18.327 trillion lire in January, Assogestioni, the industry body said.</p>
<p>But equity funds saw a rise in net inflow, to 2.345 trillion lire from 1.795 trillion lire in January.  </p>
<p>					February 1997     January 1997</p>
<p> Redemptions (bln lire)	     11,467	   10,227</p>
<p> Subscriptions			  26,387	   28,554</p>
<p>Net inflow, outflow (-) from:</p>
<p> Equity funds			    2,345	    1,795</p>
<p>     of which Italian		     83		457</p>
<p> Bond funds			     12,087	   16,144</p>
<p> Mixed funds				 487		388</p>
<p>-- Milan bureau +392 66129450</p>
</text>
